0193: the front camera's frames reach the CSID (bluecam_stream=2)

camcc PLL3 at 384 MHz; cphy_rx and the IFE-lite CSID clock from it, the
CSIPHY2 timer at 192 MHz (PLL3/2); L1A and L26A voted on (the PHY's
supplies, shared with the display PHY, left on); CSIPHY2 with Linux's
SDM845 lane table (4 data lanes, settle count 11, bluecam_settle=N); the
IFE-lite CSID reset, RX on PHY 2 with 4 lanes, RDI0 for RAW10. Before the
sensor starts, the CSID's own test pattern runs for 300 ms as a check.
While the sensor streams, the CSID's RX and RDI0 interrupt status is
polled for 1 s and counted per bit (no interrupt handler, no IFE output
yet). Everything but the two rails is put back after.

